WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.191
In this video, you will enter your home in a neighborhood contest.

00:00:04.191 --> 00:00:08.209
You will add photos, your address, and a name, and agree to the rules.

00:00:08.209 --> 00:00:09.850
It takes just a few minutes.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:10.981
We start on the map.

00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:13.632
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.777
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:19.527 --> 00:00:20.508
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.271 --> 00:00:26.960
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.155
See the three dots?

00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:32.458
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:32.996
Tap them.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.414
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:43.190
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:47.239
Under Live now, find the contest, and tap Enter my home.

00:00:49.051 --> 00:00:54.602
If you are not signed in yet, the site asks you to sign in, with Google, or with your email.

00:00:54.602 --> 00:00:58.303
That keeps one person from entering the same home many times.

00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:00.571
This video picks up after you sign in.

00:01:01.279 --> 00:01:02.130
First, photos.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:06.273
Show the lights at their best, so take them at night with everything on.

00:01:06.273 --> 00:01:07.295
Tap Choose photos.

00:01:09.147 --> 00:01:13.755
You can pick several, and the first one becomes the cover photo that people see first.

00:01:14.661 --> 00:01:15.579
Tap Next.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:18.753
Next, your address.

00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:21.129
Type your street address and ZIP code.

00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:29.290
This is where the pin goes on the map, and visitors will see it so they can drive by, so only enter an address you are happy to share.

00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:32.385
Now the name to show.

00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:36.632
This is how your entry appears to voters, for example, The Kim family.

00:01:36.632 --> 00:01:41.417
You can add a line about your display, like, the roof is synchronized to music.

00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:44.168
It is optional, but it helps neighbors choose.

00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:48.589
The last screen lists what you entered.

00:01:48.589 --> 00:01:51.772
Each line has an Edit link, if you spot a mistake.

00:01:51.772 --> 00:01:56.203
Tick the box to agree to the official rules, which you can read first.

00:01:56.203 --> 00:01:57.763
Then tap Submit my entry.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.486
You are entered!

00:02:01.486 --> 00:02:07.278
The organizer reviews every entry before it goes on the map, so it may take a little while to appear.

00:02:07.278 --> 00:02:09.720
You will get an email when it is approved.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.787
And you can come back to edit it, which we cover next.

00:02:13.794 --> 00:02:16.077
Next up: Edit or withdraw your entry.
